==English==
{{Webster 1913}}

===Etymology 1===
{{rfe|lang=en}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[wooden]] [[block]], the size of a [[brick]], built into a [[wall]], as a [[hold]] for the [[nail]]s of [[woodwork]].
# One of the [[square]] [[log]]s of [[wood]] used in a [[pile]] to [[support]] the [[roof]] of a [[mine]].
# {{context|shipbuilding|lang=en}} A [[treenail]] to [[fasten]] the [[shore]]s.

====Verb====
{{en-verb|nogg}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} to [[fill in]], as between [[scantling]], with [[brickwork]].
# {{context|transitive|shipbuilding|lang=en}} to fasten, as [[shores]], with [[treenails]].


===Etymology 2===

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# Short for [[noggin]].


===Etymology 3===

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# Short for [[eggnog]].
# {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} A kind of strong [[ale]].
#: {{rfquotek|Halliwell}}

===Etymology 4===

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|offensive|derogatory|ethnic slur|lang=en}} A dark-skinned person; [[nig-nog]].
# {{context|AU|dated|ethnic slur|lang=en}} A Vietnamese person.

